Tau runs and measures third-party models and uses third-party libraries. Their
licences are their own:

- Laya (Convai Innovations), convaiinnovations/laya: Apache License 2.0
- Von (wfzyx/von): Apache License 2.0
- ModernBERT (Answer.AI) and mmBERT (JHU CLSP) encoders, which the models above
  are built on: Apache License 2.0 and MIT respectively, per their model cards
- ONNX Runtime (Microsoft): MIT License
- Tokenizers.DotNet (sappho192), wrapping Hugging Face tokenizers: MIT / Apache License 2.0

- OpenTelemetry .NET (OpenTelemetry Authors): Apache License 2.0
- YamlDotNet (Antoine Aubry and contributors): MIT License

Tau measures its models on two datasets, downloaded by scripts and not
redistributed here:

- Banking77 (Casanueva et al., 2020, PolyAI): CC BY 4.0
- Tobi-Bueck/customer-support-tickets: CC BY-NC 4.0 (non-commercial). Only
  measurements and calibrators are published, never ticket rows.

Model weights aren't redistributed in this repository. Scripts download them
from their original locations at pinned revisions.

THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md lists every package, model and dataset with its
version, licence and source.
